let __v_58 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"sprain\",{\"$tuple\":[\"It depends how bad it is. A mild sprain is usually much better in one to two weeks and normal again in four to six; a bad one with a lot of bruising can take eight to twelve weeks, and the first 48 hours of rest, ice and keeping it raised are what set that up. Start gentle movement and walking on it as the pain allows rather than staying off it, and get it seen if you cannot put weight on it at all, it is very swollen, or it is no better after a week.\",\"Most sprains are much better in one to two weeks and properly right in four to six; a bad one can take a couple of months. Ice and rest for the first two days, then gentle walking and moving it as far as it lets you. A joint you cannot put weight on, or one that is no better after a week, is worth having looked at.\"]}],[\"burn\",{\"$tuple\":[\"A small burn usually settles in a week to ten days, and a blistering one takes about two to three weeks to heal from underneath. Keep it clean and covered and leave blisters alone; anything bigger than your palm, on the face or hands, or slow to heal after two weeks should be seen.\",\"A small burn is mostly fine in seven to ten days, and a blistered one in about two to three weeks. Leave the blisters alone and keep it covered; a burn that is not healing after a fortnight, or is on the face or hands, needs a nurse.\"]}],[\"blister\",{\"$tuple\":[\"A rubbed blister drains and dries up in about three to five days and the skin under it is new in a week or two; leave the roof on, cover it with a padded plaster and keep it dry. One that is hot, spreading or weeping pus is the doctor's rather than time.\",\"Most blisters settle in three to five days and are properly new skin in a week or two. Cover it, don't pop it, and keep it dry; hot, spreading or pus needs a doctor.\"]}],[\"cut\",{\"$tuple\":[\"A small cut closes over in a few days and is usually fully healed in a week or two, with the edges kept together and the dressing changed. Redness spreading, pus, or a cut that gapes needs to be seen the same day rather than waited on.\",\"Small cuts close in a few days and are properly healed in a week or two. Keep it clean and covered, and get it looked at if it goes red and hot, weeps pus, or will not close.\"]}],[\"sunburn\",{\"$tuple\":[\"The redness of sunburn usually settles in three to five days and the peeling in about a week. Cool showers, plenty of water and leaving the peeling skin alone are what help; shivering, dizziness or bad blisters need a doctor.\",\"Sunburn redness mostly fades in three to five days and the peeling takes about a week. Cool showers and water help, and leave the skin alone; shivery, dizzy or badly blistered is a doctor.\"]}]]}")?;
